      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 3d/hero-from-photos\n\nOne Klein still -> one textured hero mesh: structure, shape, the 1024 upsample, then the texture pass paints the geometry. This is the entry point of the lane when you have a single good plate and want a single good asset.\n\nSource: `LoadImage` with a Klein still (`ez_still_*.png` or a clay plate). The App row exposes the source image, the upsample `target_resolution`, the texture pass steps, and the `SaveGLB` prefix, so a Run can be retuned without opening the graph.\n\nUNET: `trellis_2_int8_convrot.safetensors`. CLIP vision: `dino_v3_vit_l.safetensors` (DINOv3 license, opt-in pack). Structure decode stays at 32.\n\nUpsample `target_resolution` is an int and ComfyUI only accepts 1024-2048 in steps of 128; this graph runs the 1024 floor.\n\nBatch stays 1 and the mesh converts through MeshToFile3D, which keeps only batch item 0 - raise the batch on `3d/character-batch` instead. SaveGLB writes the mesh to `output/assets/objects/_lab-hero/hero_NNNNN_.glb`; MeshToFile3D only converts in memory. Do not mint an Asset Bible row from this graph.\n\nQueue `3d/multi-image-asset` when one plate is not enough and the object needs several views fused.\n\nDINOv3 is Meta's custom commercial-friendly license - not Apache. MIT TRELLIS weights without DINOv3 cannot Queue.\n\nOccupancy: trellis - stop Blender desk, LTX, Wan, Klein denoise. One GB10 job.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Operator note"
    },
